00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:18.040
And kind of along with that came a kind of theoretical model that was really highly motivated by kind of the scientific method.

98
00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:27.320
So you had these experts who were designing their own tracking tools and they would ask these questions and then you know run experiments and then evaluate those experiments and then act on them.

99
00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:40.920
Around the time that we were thinking around about the lived informatics, that's where we started to see these Apple watches and Fitbits and really like mobile apps, kind of uh broadly popular versions of self-tracking or personal informatics popping up.

100
00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:51.000
And so we kind of looked back at what we had understood about how and why people are tracking with with kind of a broader lens of, you know, now significantly more people are tracking.

